{
  "sample": "internet-go-echo-realworld",
  "$comment": "Hand-labeled from the pinned sample source (scripts/samples.json), not from Concentrate output. echo v4 with jinzhu/gorm (v1) and sqlite. Routes: every route main.go and handler/routes.go register; Register runs on the /api group main.go creates, and a route path \"\" is the group's path. Calls: every call site in the production Go files (handler/*_test.go and the generated docs/docs.go excluded) whose callee is a function or method of this repository, with the function it runs; calls into echo, gorm, jwt-go, validator and other dependencies (c.Bind, c.Validate, gorm.IsRecordNotFoundError), and calls of local closures (extractor), function-typed fields (config.Skipper) and parameters (next) are not labeled, so any target they get counts as a false positive. A call on the user.Store or article.Store interface (h.userStore.GetByID) is labeled with the method of its only production implementation (store.UserStore, store.ArticleStore). Data access: each store method's gorm chains, by the model the chain queries (Model(), else the method's value, else the Where struct), the models its Preload paths name, and the model an Association(\"Field\") reaches (Find / Count read; Append / Replace / Delete update); tables are gorm v1's names. Where the chain's Preload paths are not fields of the chain's model but of the associated one (ListByTag, ListByWhoFavorited: Model(&tag).Preload(\"Author\")...Association(\"Articles\")), the preloads are labeled as reads of the associated model's related models, which gorm runs. AutoMigrate creates tables and is not an access. Env: the production code reads no environment variable (the JWT secret is a constant), so any env read found is a false positive.",
